triage: fix_game: The rules are sound and the tests read them correctly. The game never offered the flek poll options, so each player's `offer` list stayed empty, every answer defaulted to NO and the multiplier stayed at 1. Per-seat options in a simultaneous poll are within the platform's capabilities, so this is an implementation error.
step C: building the game file
step D: evaluating
triage: revise_rules: The game was built as specified, and evaluation shows two design flaws. Each round has five choice steps (bid, flek poll, three cards), over the limit of four. A thoughtless first-option policy, which most likely amounts to always passing and never fleking, wins about 95% of matches, while the last option (always bidding the highest contract) almost always loses. Bidding as designed punishes declaring far more than it rewards it.
