triage: revise_rules: The game was built and behaves as specified, but the design itself fails evaluation. It needs 6 choice steps per round, over the limit of 4. A fixed thoughtless policy also dominates: always taking the first option (PASS, then the lowest-ranked choices) wins about 88% of decided matches, and always taking the last option (bid 60) almost always loses.

